WEBVTT

NOTE week06-clip2-contrastive-learning
NOTE Narration read by an AI-generated voice.
NOTE The clip has its own caption along the bottom of the frame, so these cues
NOTE are placed near the top to keep the two from overlapping.

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.422 line:2 align:center
Contrastive learning starts by making
two different views of the same ECG,

2
00:00:05.422 --> 00:00:08.617 line:2 align:center
using random augmentations.

3
00:00:08.817 --> 00:00:11.929 line:2 align:center
Here, view one is cropped
and has added noise,

4
00:00:11.929 --> 00:00:16.883 line:2 align:center
and view two is rescaled with a slow
baseline drift. The heart rhythm,

5
00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:20.550 line:2 align:center
and so the diagnosis, stays the same.

6
00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:24.694 line:2 align:center
Both views pass through the same
encoder, with shared weights.

7
00:00:24.694 --> 00:00:29.350 line:2 align:center
Each view becomes one point
in the embedding space.

8
00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:36.859 line:2 align:center
In practice we train on a batch, so the
other ECGs in the batch, here B, C, and D,

9
00:00:36.859 --> 00:00:39.350 line:2 align:center
also become points.

10
00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:43.091 line:2 align:center
Training pulls the two views
of ECG A toward each other,

11
00:00:43.091 --> 00:00:47.350 line:2 align:center
and pushes the other ECGs
in the batch further away.

12
00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:50.184 line:2 align:center
The loss turns this into a classification.

13
00:00:50.184 --> 00:00:56.472 line:2 align:center
Compare A1 with every other view in the
batch, apply a softmax, and its partner,

14
00:00:56.472 --> 00:01:00.683 line:2 align:center
A2, should win, here with 0.59.

15
00:01:00.883 --> 00:01:05.861 line:2 align:center
This is the InfoNCE loss. It is
a softmax over the similarities,

16
00:01:05.861 --> 00:01:09.050 line:2 align:center
each divided by a temperature tau,

17
00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:14.283 line:2 align:center
and we minimize the negative log
probability of the true partner.

18
00:01:14.483 --> 00:01:17.376 line:2 align:center
After training on many unlabeled ECGs,

19
00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:21.316 line:2 align:center
recordings with similar rhythms
tend to land close together,

20
00:01:21.316 --> 00:01:25.883 line:2 align:center
even though the model never
saw a single diagnosis.

21
00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:31.862 line:2 align:center
For pathology tiles, the two views come
from random crops, flips and rotations,

22
00:01:31.862 --> 00:01:33.819 line:2 align:center
and changes in stain color,

23
00:01:33.819 --> 00:01:39.813 line:2 align:center
because tissue has no fixed orientation
and staining varies between labs.
